INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'ai-training-jobs-software-engineers-20261104', 'global', 'USA',
'AI Training Jobs for Software Engineers: 374 Roles Paying $40 to $150 an Hour',
'',
'As of 4 November 2026, 374 AI training roles for software engineers are open across 27 platforms, with typical pay of $40 to $150 an hour and a median of $65 an hour.',
'',
$$<p>As of 4 November 2026, AI training jobs for software engineers number 374 open roles across 27 AI training platforms, with typical pay running from $40 to $150 an hour and a median of $65 an hour, according to a live count checked against each platform's own job board every hour. AI training jobs for software engineers are hourly contract roles in which engineers review and rank the code a model writes, write coding tasks with the tests a correct answer must pass, and fix a model's failed attempts in real repositories. The highest advertised rate in the count is $400 an hour, at micro1, but most roles sit far below that ceiling, and 52 of the 374 roles state no hourly rate at all, so the headline figures describe only the roles that publish pay.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Count date</th><td>4 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Open roles for software engineers</th><td>374, across 27 AI training platforms</td></tr>
<tr><th>Typical hourly pay</th><td>$40 to $150 an hour, median $65</td></tr>
<tr><th>Highest advertised rate</th><td>$400 an hour, at micro1</td></tr>
<tr><th>Roles stating pay</th><td>322 of 374; 52 state no hourly rate</td></tr>
<tr><th>Rates measured</th><td>258 distinct advertised rates, across 22 platforms</td></tr>
<tr><th>Work type</th><td>Remote, hourly contract work; hours depend on the project</td></tr>
<tr><th>Usual first step</th><td>A coding assessment or a paid trial task</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>None; a legitimate platform never charges you to apply</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>AI training jobs: what the work actually involves</h2>
<p>The work splits into distinct kinds of tasks, and the count groups the 374 roles accordingly. Code review, evaluation and agentic coding account for 77 roles: reviewing, ranking and grading code a model writes, auditing the step-by-step traces of coding agents, and building tasks in the style of SWE-Bench from real repositories, with tests a fix has to pass. A further 95 roles are open to software engineers in any language, covering writing and fixing code to the tasks a project sets, checking a model's solutions and explaining what it got wrong. Python accounts for 33 roles, JavaScript, TypeScript and full-stack work for 48 roles, and other languages including Java, C++, Go, Rust and mobile development for 79 roles. A further 42 roles cover data science and machine learning, where engineers check a model's analyses, experiments and code and design the evaluations it is tested on.</p>
<p>Most roles start with a coding assessment or a paid trial task, and many ask for a GitHub profile or years of professional experience in the language they name. The count's own guidance adds a warning for employed engineers: check the outside-work and intellectual property clauses of an existing contract before starting, and never use an employer's code or credentials in a task. The work is usually part time and flexible, but hours depend on the project, and a project can end without warning.</p>
<h2>AI training jobs: who pays what, platform by platform</h2>
<p>The platform table shows how wide the pay spread is. SuperAnnotate lists 49 roles at up to $120 an hour, Alignerr lists 46 roles at $20 to $400 an hour, and Invisible lists 44 roles at $6 to $150 an hour. Micro1 lists 32 roles at $20 to $400 an hour, Anyone AI lists 32 roles at $15 to $150 an hour, and Turing lists 29 roles at $100 to $150 an hour. AfterQuery lists 26 roles at $45 to $175 an hour, Weekday lists 16 roles at $20 to $230 an hour, and Mercor lists 15 roles at $50 to $180 an hour. At the smaller end, RemoExperts lists 6 roles at $50 to $150 an hour, Surge AI lists 1 role at $100 to $150 an hour, and DataAnnotation lists 9 roles at $40 to $150 an hour.</p>
<p>Read those ranges with care. A range such as $20 to $400 an hour does not mean a typical engineer earns near the top of it; the count's own typical band of $40 to $150 an hour, with a $65 median, is the better guide, measured from 258 distinct advertised rates and excluding 64 roles that advertise only a maximum rate such as "up to $X an hour". The platform list is also ordered by what applying is worth, with a referral boost for platforms that pay the source a referral fee, so position on the list is not a neutral ranking of quality. Pay is set by the platform, not by the listing site.</p>
<p>The wider research behind the count puts software engineering in context. In the source's field-level research, software and IT counted 406 open roles on 3 November 2026 across 28 platforms, up 4.9 per cent, against 2,442 people with profiles in the field, or 6.0 people per role. That is a competitive market: many engineers are chasing each role, and the assessment stage is where most applications end.</p>
<h2>AI training jobs: how to apply, and what to do next</h2>
<p>Start on the platform's own job board, and confirm three things before spending time on an assessment: the language and stack the project actually wants, the country and credential rules for that project, and the pay terms for the specific role, including whether the rate is fixed or a range and how hours are approved. A strong engineer in the wrong stack or the wrong country will not pass the first screen. Keep a record of each application, the role text and the rate stated, because listings change and roles close without notice.</p>
<p>For engineers already in full-time work, settle the contract question first, since a conflict over outside work or intellectual property can cost more than the extra income is worth.</p>
<p>Finally, a legitimate platform never charges you to apply or to get work, and any message asking for a fee for training, equipment or onboarding is a warning sign. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-startup-jobs-13514-roles-20261104">Growentix reported on 4 November 2026 that 1,100 AI startups were advertising 13,514 roles</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-jobs-india-hiring-october-naukri-jobspeak-20261103">Indian AI hiring rose in October 2026 even as overall hiring stayed uneven</a>. AI training work is the contract, hourly side of that same market: flexible and genuinely paid, but competitive and worth checking role by role on the platform's own page.</p>
<p><small>Sources: AITraining.jobs, "AI Training Jobs for Software Engineers", figures as of 4 November 2026, checked against each platform's job board; field-level research "Expert Fields in Demand for AI Training" and "AI Training Talent: Supply and Demand", data from 7 October 2026 to 3 November 2026.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://aitraining.jobs/ai-training-jobs-for-software-engineers'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'dsssb-delhi-court-641-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'DSSSB Recruitment 2026: 641 Delhi Court Posts, Applications Close 4 November at 11 PM',
'',
'DSSSB Advertisement No. 04/2026 for 641 posts in the Delhi District Courts and Family Courts closes at 11:00 PM on 4 November 2026; applicants must be citizens of India.',
'',
$$<p>On 4 November 2026, the application window closes at 11:00 PM for DSSSB Recruitment 2026, the DSSSB combined examination for 641 posts in the Delhi District Courts and Family Courts. DSSSB Recruitment 2026, under Advertisement No. 04/2026 dated 30 September 2026, covers Senior Personal Assistant, Personal Assistant, Junior Judicial Assistant, Process Server and Peon, Orderly and Dak Peon posts, and applications are accepted online only through dsssbonline.nic.in. Candidates must be citizens of India, and qualifications and experience are judged as on 4 November 2026, the closing date.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Recruiting body</th><td>Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board (DSSSB), on behalf of Delhi District Courts and Family Courts</td></tr>
<tr><th>Advertisement</th><td>No. 04/2026, dated 30 September 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Total posts</th><td>641 (tentative, including backlog)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>6 October 2026, 12:00 noon, to 4 November 2026, 11:00 PM</td></tr>
<tr><th>How to apply</th><td>Online only, through dsssbonline.nic.in</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>18 to 27 years as on 1 June 2026, with relaxations for reserved categories</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>Rs. 100 for UR, OBC and EWS male candidates; exempt for women, SC, ST, PwBD and ex-servicemen candidates</td></tr>
<tr><th>Fee payment</th><td>SBI e-Pay only; fee once paid is non-refundable</td></tr>
<tr><th>Exam date</th><td>Not announced; to be intimated later on DSSSB and Delhi District Courts websites</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>DSSSB Recruitment 2026: post-wise vacancies and eligibility</h2>
<p>The 641 tentative vacancies break down as Senior Personal Assistant 27, Personal Assistant 206 (189 in District and Sessions Courts and 17 in Family Courts), Junior Judicial Assistant 174 (151 in District and Sessions Courts and 23 in Family Courts), Process Server 92 (91 in District and Sessions Courts and 1 in Family Courts), and Peon, Orderly and Dak Peon 142 (139 in District and Sessions Courts and 3 in Family Courts). The board states that the vacancies are tentative and may increase or decrease.</p>
<p>Eligibility differs sharply by post, and the shorthand and typing speeds decide the assistant posts. Senior Personal Assistant requires a degree, shorthand at 110 words per minute and typing at 40 words per minute. Personal Assistant requires a degree, shorthand at 100 words per minute, typing at 40 words per minute and knowledge of computers. Junior Judicial Assistant requires a degree and typing at not less than 40 words per minute on a computer. Process Server requires Matriculation or equivalent, or Higher Secondary, plus a valid light motor vehicle licence and two years of unblemished driving experience, while Peon, Orderly and Dak Peon requires Matriculation or equivalent from a recognised board. Ineligibility found at document verification leads to rejection for that post code with no reallocation.</p>
<p>The age limit is 18 to 27 years as on 1 June 2026, meaning candidates must have been born not earlier than 2 June 1999 and not later than 1 June 2008. Relaxation is 5 years for SC and ST candidates, 3 years for OBC candidates, 10 years for PwBD candidates in the unreserved and EWS categories, 15 years for PwBD candidates in SC and ST categories, 13 years for PwBD candidates in OBC categories, and military service plus 3 years for ex-servicemen, up to a maximum age of 55 years. The date of birth in the Matriculation certificate available at application time is final.</p>
<h2>DSSSB Recruitment 2026: pay scales and selection process</h2>
<p>Pay follows the post's group. Senior Personal Assistant carries Rs. 9,300 to Rs. 34,800 plus grade pay of Rs. 4,800 in Group B (non-gazetted), and Personal Assistant carries the same basic scale plus grade pay of Rs. 4,600, also in Group B. Junior Judicial Assistant carries Rs. 5,200 to Rs. 20,200 plus grade pay of Rs. 2,800 in Group C, Process Server the same basic scale plus grade pay of Rs. 2,400, and Peon, Orderly and Dak Peon the same basic scale plus grade pay of Rs. 2,000.</p>
<p>Selection runs through separate examinations for each post code, with minimum qualifying marks of 50 per cent for unreserved and EWS candidates and 45 per cent for OBC (Delhi), SC, ST, PwBD and ex-servicemen candidates. Each multiple-choice question carries 1 mark, with negative marking of 0.25 for each wrong answer. For Senior Personal Assistant and Personal Assistant, Tier I is a 90-mark multiple-choice test over 90 minutes, Tier II is a 75-mark descriptive English test over 90 minutes, Tier III is a qualifying shorthand, transcription and typing skill test, and Tier IV is a 10-mark interview, with final merit on Tier II and Tier IV.</p>
<p>Junior Judicial Assistant follows a similar pattern with a 120-mark Tier I test, a 100-mark descriptive Tier II test, a qualifying typing test at 40 words per minute, and a 15-mark interview, with final merit on Tier II and Tier IV combined. Process Server faces a 100-mark bilingual objective test covering English, Hindi, general knowledge and arithmetic, a qualifying driving test in real traffic conditions, and a 15-mark interview. Peon, Orderly and Dak Peon faces a 100-mark bilingual objective test on the same four subjects, followed by a 15-mark interview.</p>
<h2>DSSSB Recruitment 2026: how to apply before 11:00 PM on 4 November 2026, and what to do next</h2>
<p>Register once on dsssbonline.nic.in if not already registered with DSSSB, then log in and apply for the chosen post code between 6 October 2026 at 12:00 noon and 4 November 2026 at 11:00 PM. Fill in all details carefully, because no correction or modification, including a category change, is allowed after final submission. Upload a recent colour photograph on a plain white or off-white background and a signature in the prescribed format, pay the applicable fee, if any, only through SBI e-Pay, and submit well before the closing time.</p>
<p>After submission, the work shifts to preparation and to watching for the examination schedule, which has not been announced. Supporting documents are sought only at the e-dossier stage after shortlisting, and scrutiny is carried out by Delhi District Courts rather than DSSSB; candidates who fail to upload the e-dossier within the given time are not considered further. Keep ready the Matriculation certificate, degree and shorthand or typing certificates, a light motor vehicle licence and proof of two years of driving experience for Process Server, and category, disability or discharge certificates where claimed.</p>
<p>The closing-hour warning applies across court recruitments this week. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/punjab-court-clerk-1270-posts-20261104">Growentix reported that the Punjab Court Clerk Recruitment 2026 for 1,270 posts also closed on 4 November 2026, at 4:00 PM</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/supreme-court-junior-court-attendant-130-posts-20261104">the Supreme Court Junior Court Attendant recruitment opened on 4 November 2026 and runs to 25 November 2026</a>. A form left at the payment step after 11:00 PM on 4 November 2026 does not count, and the official notification remains the final word.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board, Advertisement No. 04/2026 dated 30 September 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert; official application portal dsssbonline.nic.in; official website dsssb.delhi.gov.in.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/dsssb-delhi-district-courts-recruitment-2026-notification-out-apply-online-for-641-posts-3070579', 'https://dsssbonline.nic.in'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'hprca-teacher-2423-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'HPRCA Teacher Recruitment 2026: 2,423 Posts, Applications Open 10 November',
'',
'HPRCA Advertisement No. 14/2026 offers 2,423 teacher posts in Himachal Pradesh CBSE-affiliated government schools; applications open 10 November 2026 and close 5 December 2026, at a fixed honorarium of Rs. 30,000 a month for 10 months a year.',
'',
$$<p>Himachal Pradesh Rajya Chayan Aayog (HPRCA), Hamirpur, has released Advertisement No. 14/2026 dated 2 November 2026 for 2,423 teacher posts in government schools affiliated to the Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE), under the Directorate of School Education, Himachal Pradesh. HPRCA teacher recruitment 2026 covers 15 subjects, from English and Mathematics to Computer, Music and Fine Arts, and online applications open on 10 November 2026 at 10:00 AM and close on 5 December 2026 at 11:59 PM through hprca.hp.gov.in. The posts are temporary, scheme-based engagements for five years with a fixed honorarium, not regular government appointments, and selected teachers will have no right to regularisation.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Recruiting body</th><td>Himachal Pradesh Rajya Chayan Aayog (HPRCA), Hamirpur</td></tr>
<tr><th>Department</th><td>Directorate of School Education, Himachal Pradesh</td></tr>
<tr><th>Advertisement</th><td>No. 14/2026, dated 2 November 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Total posts</th><td>2,423 across 15 subjects (subject-wise figures add up to 2,423; vacancies tentative)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Post codes</th><td>26046 to 26060</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application window</th><td>10 November 2026, 10:00 AM, to 5 December 2026, 11:59 PM</td></tr>
<tr><th>Honorarium</th><td>Rs. 30,000 per month, payable for 10 months in an academic year</td></tr>
<tr><th>Engagement</th><td>Temporary, scheme-based, for five years; no regularisation</td></tr>
<tr><th>Age limit</th><td>18 to 45 years as on 1 January 2026</td></tr>
<tr><th>Application fee</th><td>Rs. 800 for all categories (Rs. 100 examination fee plus Rs. 700 processing fee)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Selection</th><td>Computer Based Test or written screening test of 120 marks, then document verification</td></tr>
<tr><th>How to apply</th><td>Online only, through hprca.hp.gov.in</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>HPRCA teacher recruitment 2026: subject-wise vacancies</h2>
<p>Mathematics carries the largest share, with 281 posts, followed by English, Hindi, Biology, Sanskrit, Commerce and Physical Education with 187 posts each. Political Science, History and Economics carry 156 posts each, while Physics, Chemistry, Computer and Music carry 95 posts each, and Fine Arts carries 172 posts. Candidates must select the correct post code when applying.</p>
<p>The category-wise summary divides the 2,423 posts as General or Unreserved 928, Economically Weaker Section 310, Scheduled Caste 582, Other Backward Classes 484 and Scheduled Tribe 119. The notification states that reservation benefits are governed by Himachal Pradesh government rules, and candidates belonging to reserved categories of other states will be considered under the General or Unreserved category. The vacancy figures are tentative and may increase or decrease according to departmental requirements.</p>
<p>The honorarium needs plain explanation. Selected teachers receive a fixed Rs. 30,000 per month for 10 months in an academic year, which amounts to Rs. 3,00,000 over those 10 months, and the engagement runs for five years under the government's teacher engagement scheme. The honorarium is not a regular government teacher pay scale, and it should not be represented as a guaranteed 12-month salary. Applicants who need year-round income should plan for the two months in each academic year when the honorarium is not payable.</p>
<h2>HPRCA teacher recruitment 2026: eligibility, age and fee</h2>
<p>Most subjects require a relevant Master's degree, a B.Ed. and a qualifying Teacher Eligibility Test (TET), with the exact conditions, including minimum marks and subject combinations, prescribed for each post code. English and Mathematics teachers need a Master's degree in the subject with prescribed graduation marks, a B.Ed. or accepted integrated teacher-education qualification, and the prescribed TET. Science teachers need a Master's degree in the relevant discipline with a B.Ed. and TET, and Commerce teachers need a Master's degree in Commerce, Accountancy, Financial Accountancy, Income Tax or a related notified specialisation with a B.Ed. and TET.</p>
<p>Some posts offer alternative routes. Computer Teacher can be reached through a B.E. or B.Tech. in Computer Science or Information Technology with prescribed marks, a B.E. or B.Tech. in any stream with a recognised postgraduate diploma in Computer Science, Technology or Applications, an M.Sc. in Computer Science or MCA with prescribed marks, a postgraduate degree in Mathematics or Physics with a postgraduate diploma in Computer Science or Computer Applications, or a DOEACC 'B' or 'C' level qualification, along with the prescribed proficiency requirement for teaching in Hindi and English. Physical Education Teacher accepts a B.P.Ed., B.P.E., integrated Physical Education degree or another prescribed NCTE-recognised qualification, and Fine Arts Teacher accepts a recognised Master's degree in Fine Arts or Visual Arts, or certain recognised Fine Arts or Painting diplomas following Higher Secondary education, subject to course duration and marks requirements.</p>
<p>The age limit is 18 to 45 years as on 1 January 2026, with upper-age relaxation for eligible reserved category candidates according to the provisions applicable to their category. Educational qualifications must be held by 5 December 2026, the last date for applications. The application fee is Rs. 800 for all categories, made up of a Rs. 100 examination fee and a Rs. 700 processing fee, payable online through credit card, debit card or net banking using the official payment gateway. The fees are non-refundable, and a correction fee of Rs. 100 applies if the application correction facility is used; HPRCA will provide a four-day correction window after the application period, with the exact schedule to be confirmed on the official website.</p>
<h2>HPRCA teacher recruitment 2026: selection, exam pattern and how to apply</h2>
<p>Selection rests on a Computer Based Test or written screening test carrying 120 marks, followed by verification of the prescribed eligibility documents. The screening examination contains 120 objective-type multiple-choice questions carrying one mark each, over 90 minutes, and candidates are ranked according to examination performance and the applicable selection rules. The notification does not prescribe a separate interview as a general selection stage, and the examination date and admit card release date have not been announced, so applicants should watch hprca.hp.gov.in after applying.</p>
<p>Apply only through the official HPRCA portal at hprca.hp.gov.in, and note that the window does not open until 10 November 2026 at 10:00 AM. Before that date, the useful work is reading the full advertisement, confirming the post code and the exact qualification conditions for that code, and gathering degree, B.Ed. and TET certificates, category certificates where claimed, and a photograph and signature in the prescribed format. When the window opens, complete the Online Recruitment Application, pay the Rs. 800 fee through the official payment gateway, and keep the submitted form and payment receipt, since the fee is non-refundable.</p>
<p>Teacher recruitment on this scale is worth comparing with other current drives before choosing where to apply. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/upessc-prt-assistant-teacher-12405-posts-20261103">Growentix covered the UPESSC assistant teacher recruitment for 12,405 posts, which closed on 4 November 2026</a>, and <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/punjab-court-clerk-1270-posts-20261104">the Punjab Court Clerk Recruitment 2026 for 1,270 posts also closed on 4 November 2026</a>. The Himachal drive differs in one respect that matters most: it is a five-year temporary engagement at a fixed honorarium, not a permanent post. Candidates who want classroom experience in Himachal Pradesh government schools have until 5 December 2026 at 11:59 PM to apply, through hprca.hp.gov.in only.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Himachal Pradesh Rajya Chayan Aayog, Advertisement No. 14/2026 dated 2 November 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert; official portal hprca.hp.gov.in.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/hprca-recruitment-2026-teacher-3077937', 'https://hprca.hp.gov.in/'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;
